<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bruno of Schauenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1205–1281</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bruno of Schauenburg was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olomouc">Olomouc</a> from 1245 to 1281, a German noble from Holstein who became the chief adviser of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottokar-ii-of-bohemia">Ottokar II of Bohemia</a>. He promoted the settlement of German colonists in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, founding villages and towns under German law, among them <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kromeriz">Kroměříž</a>. He also took part in Ottokar's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> against the pagan Prussians.</p></div>
